# Bid card Chat / Bid rules

Use [BidCardActionRules](lib/core/utils/bid_card_action_rules.dart) as the single source of truth. Do not duplicate visibility logic in screens.

## Product rules (locked in)

| Post type | Chat | Bid button | Who can submit bid |
|-----------|------|------------|-------------------|
| **Customer job** (customer poster) | Non-owners when open; artists always on detail | **Artists only** (always on detail for artists) | Tattoo artists only (open requests) |
| **Promo** (artist poster) | Non-owners when open | Customers only when open | Customers only (open requests) |
| **Own post** | Hidden | Hidden | — |
| **Closed promo / closed job (customer viewer)** | Hidden | Hidden | — |

## Implementation

- `showChat`, `showBidButton`, and `canSubmitBid` come from `BidCardActionRules`.
- **Explore cards do not show Chat/Bid buttons** — tap a card to open [BidDetailPage](lib/screens/bid_detail_page.dart), where buttons live.
- On detail, `_showPlaceBidDialog` must gate on `canSubmitBid`, not `showBidButton` alone.
- Server enforcement stays in [BidService.placeBid](lib/core/services/bid_service.dart).

## Do not change without explicit request

- Artists bidding on customer jobs only.
- Customers bidding on artist promos only.
- No Chat/Bid on own posts or closed requests.
